So mark your calendars for Friday July 25th
from 12:20PM to 1:20PM Pacific Time.

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:25.679
I'll be posting a full breakdown of any footage
they show so be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:25.679 --> 00:00:30.089
There's going to be a ton of stuff happening
that week so I'm going to be making some special

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:31.929
Comic Con specific videos starting next week.

00:00:31.929 --> 00:00:35.580
I'll explain the special giveaways I'll be
doing when I start posting those.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:41.230
Question time, so assume spoilers for everything
up to where we are on the show right now.

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:42.750
Everything through Season 4.

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:47.300
There's not a lot of comic stuff in my answers
aside from what we've already discussed like

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.210
Hunters and Father Gabriel and some behind
the scenes filming stuff in terms of locations.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.300
Everybody ready, here we go.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.240
Question 1 - Alex asks, what happened to Tara's
sister, is she ever coming back?

00:00:59.240 --> 00:01:02.870
Lilly was killed during the Governor's attack
in the aftermath.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.970
Yes she did kill the governor, that was the
last we saw of her on screen.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:10.350
It's implied that she just didn't survive
the Walker Assault that came after the survivors

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.810
took off in different directions.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:16.640
They didn't say specifically if she'd been
wounded and died from that or if she shot

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.240
herself in grief or if she went into shock
from grief and walkers got to her.

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:23.750
Based on the look in her eyes as she shot
the Governor I'm assuming that she shot herself.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.409
Her daughter was dead and the man she trusted
turned out to be a complete lie.

00:01:27.409 --> 00:01:31.030
Had Tara been there with her she might have
saved Lilly, but she wasn't.

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:35.890
So I think Lilly didn't have anything to live
for anymore and she just wanted it to be over.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:39.940
That's just my interpretation.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:44.890
Question 2 - Dominique asks Once the survivors
escape Terminus, what do you think they will

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:45.890
do?

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:49.980
Depending on when they leave Terminus or escape,
I think they'll head for Alexandria.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:57.110
For people that haven't read the comic, it's
basically Washington DC.

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:00.340
It's the place Abraham was trying to get Eugene
to.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:05.049
Based on all the behind the scenes stuff people
have been posting from the set, it seems like

00:02:05.049 --> 00:02:06.390
they're not going to get there anytime soon.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.670
I'm hoping Season 6 turns into the road to
Alexandria.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:12.670
Andrew J West's character, Gareth.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:13.670
This guy.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.160
Is a series regular this year.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:16.600
Meaning he's in most of the episodes.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:29.260
I'm hoping that means they'll spend a large
portion of the season at Terminus.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.670
Question 3 - KJ asks, what did you think about
Aisha Tyler's comment about Beth becoming

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:35.910
Gareth's Terminus Queen?

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:39.599
I don't believe it, it's a funny way to think
about Beth.

00:02:39.599 --> 00:02:41.590
She is supposed to get a lot more mature this
season.

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.810
But the only things we know about her specifically
is that she'll get her own story like the

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:47.130
Governor got in Season 4.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:51.390
There will be like a Beth episode that will
tell the story of what happened to her after

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:52.850
she got kidnapped.

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:56.569
Most of the rumors I've seen say her story
this season will mostly take place away from

00:02:56.569 --> 00:02:57.569
the survivors.

00:02:57.569 --> 00:02:59.180
But eventually I think they'll be reunited.

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:05.900
I'd love to think of a scenario where Beth
helps them escape.

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.330
Question 4 - Ash asks do you have a theory
on how Carol and Tyreese learn about Rick

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.660
with the group being trapped?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:14.800
And do you think it will be an emotional reunion?

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.000
I think they'll just arrive at Terminus after
Rick's Group gets dumped in the car.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.890
I'm hoping it's a situation where they get
to the fence line and see Gareth's men with

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:27.060
guns on Rick as they're stuffing them into
the traincar.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:34.400
Or they'll just somehow see something funky
going on and figure out that Terminus is a

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.400
bad place.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.910
I don't think they'll just waltz in the front
gate and be dumped in the train car like everyone

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:39.910
else.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:40.910
As for the actual reunion.

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.610
If they do end up going inside Terminus, yes.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:46.640
Rick is probably going to have a major joy
attack when he sees Judith.

00:03:46.640 --> 00:03:51.330
That would definitely be something to push
him over the edge and make him go crazy on

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.980
all the Termites.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.200
Question 5 - Rose asks do you think Daryl
will be happy to see that Beth is alive when

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.090
and if they meet up with everyone again?﻿

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.110
I don't think Daryl will see Beth anytime
soon, but I think it will be like Rick seeing

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:05.140
baby Judith again.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.530
Beth is definitely special to Daryl.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:09.290
They had a life changing field trip together.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:21.019
I think she brought him back from the dead,
emotionally speaking.

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:25.440
Question 6 - Galaxy Ronin asks If they're
doing flashbacks this season do you think

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:29.130
characters from the first two seasons, who
died, might make appearance?

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:34.810
I wonder if your thinking of the Morales Family.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:38.500
A lot of people were hoping they'd come back
in the Season 3 finale but they never did.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.030
I definitely think they'll be doing more flashbacks.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:45.180
But usually they're just to tell character's
backstories or to deal with periods of time

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.900
the show didn't include in the regular episodes.

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:51.860
Like when we flashed back to the Prison, that
period was from the time between the season

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:56.550
3 finale and the season 4 premiere.

00:04:56.550 --> 00:05:01.100
I think if they do a non character-specific
flashback, like a group flashback, it will

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.300
be from between seasons.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:07.530
Mostly I'm just expecting character flashbacks
like Michonne's just for characters that haven't

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:08.660
got them yet.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:13.190
Question 7 - David asks, do you think anyone
is going to buy into Gareth's new way of life

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.240
they teased?

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:19.300
I'd be disappointed if at least one survivor
didn't accidentally eat some of that grill

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.300
meat.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.610
It would be funny in a really horrifying way.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:25.180
I don't think we're going to see any brainwashed
survivors, I don't think the new Rick would

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.330
let that happen to anyone.

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:30.880
Looking at the people in this train car I
don't think any of them are so empty headed

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.139
that they'd let Gareth fill them with his
ideas.

00:05:34.139 --> 00:05:38.199
Andrew West was teasing Gareth's philosophy
in the interview he did.

00:05:38.199 --> 00:05:44.240
He made it sound like a pretty big deal, so
I think the show will tease us and make us

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.120
think some of the characters will drink the
kool aide.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:54.199
But in the end I don't think any of them are
going to go to the darkside.

00:05:54.199 --> 00:05:57.850
Question 8 - Fabian asks How much time will
the survivors spent on Terminus?

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.990
The whole season or just half of it?

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:04.460
When Andrew West was announced as a Series
Regular for Season 5 I thought that meant

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:10.009
they'd be spending at least half the season
there.

00:06:10.009 --> 00:06:15.620
All the behind the scenes pictures I've seen
from the set right now make it seem like they're

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.930
on the road in different places.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:20.380
In terms of episode production status I think
they're about halfway done filming episodes.

00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:25.080
Norman Reedus posted this picture saying "Day
1" at the beginning of May, so based on a

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:31.800
production schedule of about one episode filmed
every 6 to 8 days, I think they're at least

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.560
8 episodes in.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:38.300
There have been a lot of spoilery images of
survivors doing things on different sets.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.680
I'm not going to post them, just because they
are kind of spoilery.

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:45.880
But right now I'm going to say by the mid-season
finale they'll be out of Terminus.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.360
They could totally leave sooner though.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:51.960
I think when they do it will include a lot
of fire and walkers.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:56.360
Question 9 - Ant C asks What do you think
cause Glenn and Maggie's group to get put

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.360
in the train car?﻿

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:01.180
Yeah, they didn't really answer this in the
special.

00:07:01.180 --> 00:07:06.590
I think that Maggie probably did a Rick thing
and freaked out after seeing something fishy.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:10.800
Glenn is just as quick to action, but of the
people in that group I think Maggie would

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.720
be the first one to point a gun at the Termites.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:18.522
Question 10 - Castiel asks If Beth is with
father Gabriel, do you think those 2 will

00:07:18.522 --> 00:07:19.639
head to terminus?

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:24.280
or will they do a beth/FG episode like they
did at the end of season 4?"

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:31.729
I think Seth Gilliam's character will try
to take her somewhere else, if he really is

00:07:31.729 --> 00:07:35.470
the Father Gabriel character it will probably
be to his church where he has supplies.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:40.949
Like I said, they'll tell that Beth story
in it's own episode like the Governor's story

00:07:40.949 --> 00:07:49.599
after Woodbury.

00:07:49.599 --> 00:07:53.970
Question 11 - John asks Do you prefer the
comic or the show?

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:56.390
There's still a lot of the comic I haven't
read yet.

00:07:56.390 --> 00:07:59.020
I typically only read along around where we
are in the show.

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:01.000
I try to not read ahead too far.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.540
So I haven't read all out war or new beginning
yet.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:04.889
I guess that means I prefer the show.

00:08:04.889 --> 00:08:07.970
I started watching the show before I started
reading the comic.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:14.160
It's a big difference in the way I experience
Game of Thrones, where I am way further ahead

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:15.830
than that show.

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:20.590
Question 12 - Nathan asks Charlie who do you
think will be the first survivor/ Rick's group

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:22.000
character to bite the dust this season?

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:27.440
There have been a lot of Glenn rumors, but
given how much they've stretched out the comic

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:31.490
story to this point, I think it's possible
that none of the main characters could die

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:32.490
anytime soon.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:37.479
AMC has no reason to kill them off, and they
can demand that Scott Gimple keep them alive

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:39.749
if they really wanted to.

00:08:39.749 --> 00:08:46.709
I mean, eventually someone will have to die,
but at this point I wouldn't be surprised

00:08:46.709 --> 00:08:49.499
if they waited till the season 5 finale to
kill one of the survivors.

00:08:49.499 --> 00:08:53.779
Question 13 - Code Red asks Do you think another
group may rescue the Survivors, such as the

00:08:53.779 --> 00:08:55.549
Hilltop or the Kingdom?

00:08:55.549 --> 00:08:56.549
﻿

00:08:56.549 --> 00:08:58.579
I don't think we'll see anyone from the Kingdom.

00:08:58.579 --> 00:09:08.009
That's a place near Washington DC, it doesn't
appear till after issue 100 and we're around

00:09:08.009 --> 00:09:10.529
issue 60 in the show right now.

00:09:10.529 --> 00:09:14.279
I think if they get any outside help it will
be from the other survivors like Carol and

00:09:14.279 --> 00:09:16.879
Tyreese or Morgan will re-appear.

00:09:16.879 --> 00:09:21.660
Mostly I think their escape will be because
of something they do.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.880
I don't think it will be a deus ex machina
situation.

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.019
The Walker parade will get there eventually,
but I don't think that will be a direct cause

00:09:29.019 --> 00:09:30.019
in their escape.

00:09:30.019 --> 00:09:33.449
They'll probably just help create a distraction
for the Termites.

00:09:33.449 --> 00:09:37.949
Question 14 - Nicholas asks do you ever think
Morgan will come back?

00:09:37.949 --> 00:09:43.079
Scott Gimple said that he'd come back eventually,
but he was saying it in Season 4.

00:09:43.079 --> 00:09:47.089
He was like, not this year, but definitely
in the future.

00:09:47.089 --> 00:09:52.110
Technically it's the future, but I'm starting
to think that if we see him, it will be at

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:58.649
another big location like Alexandria.

00:09:58.649 --> 00:10:03.970
Question 15 - Daniel asks If everyone is infected
with the Virus, how come people that get bitten

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:06.230
turn super fast?

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:11.089
The walkers have all kinds of crazy super
bacteria growing in their mouths, so when

00:10:11.089 --> 00:10:16.600
someone gets bitten they get infected with
crazy batcteria that causes all kinds of crazy

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:20.699
infections that shuts down their immune systems
way faster.

00:10:20.699 --> 00:10:23.029
So it's not really related to the walker virus.

00:10:23.029 --> 00:10:26.299
It's just like getting a really bad infection
from an animal bite.

00:10:26.299 --> 00:10:32.839
Question 16 - Mess Monster asks For last 16
eps in season 4 it was all about "can you

00:10:32.839 --> 00:10:38.470
come back from during terrible things" and
know we're in season 5 what would this season

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.709
be about?

00:10:39.709 --> 00:10:46.350
They kind of explained that this season it
was all about doing what it takes to survive.

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:50.350
Like are you willing to do what it takes,
do you have it in you.

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:53.209
That's where you get the talk about people
who are not badasses, becoming badasses.

00:10:53.209 --> 00:10:55.029
It's all about stepping up to the challenge.

00:10:55.029 --> 00:10:59.790
There's so many awful things I'm looking forward
to seeing Rick and the survivors do in the

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:01.049
name of survival.

00:11:01.049 --> 00:11:07.029
Maybe for one of my future bonus videos I"ll
do a video for the top 10 most badass things

00:11:07.029 --> 00:11:08.649
the survivors have done so far.

